id: pm-web-fy9a
title: Expand pm-web coverage gate to every executable source file and all four 100% metrics
description: "The current release:check passed 408 real-Postgres and other tests, but coverage-gate reported only 32 source files with several measured branch/function percentages below 100. This does not meet the requested all-source 100/100/100/100 quality gate. The existing pm-web-9ulj issue specifically owns route-layer real-Postgres integration; this item owns gate scope and all four metrics across every executable source file."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-29T12:36:48.604Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T05:42:59.193Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "Measure and require 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines for every executable source file; retain real integration and route tests; fail when a file is omitted or coverage data is missing; avoid artificial tests or coverage exclusions."
reporter: codex
severity: medium
environment: "pm-web PR #163 release:check 2026-09-29; coverage-gate 32 reported source files"
repro_steps: npm run coverage; inspect the per-file coverage table and scripts/coverage-gate.ts source inclusion and thresholds.
expected_result: "All executable TypeScript source files are included and statements, branches, functions, and lines each measure 100% through real behavior tests."
actual_result: Current gate says thresholds met for 32 source files while several per-file metrics are below 100 and executable source outside that declared set is unmeasured.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T04:37:08.394Z",pi-glm,"Baseline recorded on branch test/full-source-coverage-gate (npm run coverage, real Postgres, V8 runtime coverage; note: statements are reported by V8 as lines for this runtime, so the line figure is the statement figure). Aggregate baseline: lines 85.00 / branches 81.40 / functions 78.58 across 33 reported src files. Per-file baselines (line%/branch%%, uncovered lines): app 95.45/80.00/90.91 (78-79 94-95 117-118 174-177 231-233); auth 96.36/87.50/100 (10-11); board 99.19/88.46/100 (49); crypto 100/100/100; csrf 100/96.00/100; db 94.47/66.67/100 (20-27 230-234); health 94.78/90.48/100 (117-118 222-226 228-229 355-365); ical 100/92.98/100; idempotency 96.14/92.38/100 (397-401 403-411 413-415); index 86.07/80.65/82.14 (27-30 196-211 277 297-298 344-399 460 491-494); middleware/auth 100; middleware/rate-limit 100; oidc 93.91/77.19/100 (136-138 161-165 170-171 229-230 299-300 315-328 404-405 434-435 441-452 567-572); routes/admin 87.04/66.67/100; routes/auth 91.22/88.68/100; routes/extensions 95.47/73.17/100 (235-246); routes/github 57.61/67.39/42.86 (130-140 157-159 193-217 257-264 289-325 330-381 429-470 475-608); routes/groups 91.45/84.78/87.50; routes/oidc 48.00/100/22.22 (46-52 65-78 91-108 147-156 163-247); routes/pm 64.20/70.14/53.47 (largest gap: ~1300 uncovered lines incl 1118-1152 1300-1355 1507-1540 1575-2538); routes/projects 85.93/85.71/100; route-helpers 100/87.50/100; route-params 100/100/100; routes/sharing 94.67/86.49/100; server 91.03/77.78/75 (48-50 54-55 76-77); fleet-snapshot 100; mutation-event-watcher 99.54/90.24/75 (90); package-catalog 100; pm-runner 94.91/82.10/87.50 (12 regions); project-watcher 98.74/86.21/78.95 (137-138 186-187); realtime-bus 93.64/76.79/78.95 (187-196 216-221); sse 93.68/94.44/91.67 (322-323 344-345 426-450); watcher-utils 100/90.91/100. Largest gaps first: routes/pm, routes/github, routes/oidc, index, pm-runner, realtime-bus, sse. Note for reproducing locally: the catalog tests derive the fleet from the package parent directory, which in a shared worktree farm holds sibling agent worktrees, so runs there need PM_FLEET_ROOT pointed at the real fleet root (documented env var in test/catalog.test.ts)."
  "2026-10-05T05:03:35.798Z",codex-sol,"Resuming the interrupted pi-glm run. Preserving and verifying its four route-contract fixes and HTTP regression tests before a focused commit. Will remeasure coverage on real disposable PostgreSQL, prioritize concurrent collaboration behavior, enforce statements explicitly, and ratchet all four thresholds. No hosted resources are in scope."
  "2026-10-05T05:13:31.541Z",codex-sol,"Fresh npm ci completed. The preserved route-contract regression suite passes 4/4 against disposable PostgreSQL and real HTTP/pm workspaces (about 36 seconds, including avoidable graph auto-sync teardown work tracked by pm-web-4fgv). The saved pre-fix run fails all four cases. Committing the recovered route fixes first; four-metric c8 measurement is in progress."
  "2026-10-05T05:17:08.162Z",codex-sol,"Fresh c8 baseline after recovered fixes: statements 86.39, branches 80.46, functions 92.11, lines 86.39 over all 33 src files; 472/476 tests pass, runtime 196.19 seconds. Four optional live-fleet catalog assertions fail because the external fleet gained pm-jev after this package snapshot. Original pi-glm baseline used Node built-in coverage (85.00 lines, 81.40 branches, 78.58 functions); c8 counts functions differently, so that change is not a test improvement. Final comparisons will use the same c8 denominator. No coverage reports were published by the failed gate."
  "2026-10-05T05:29:22.936Z",codex-sol,"The package worktree farm is not a canonical fleet: implicit sibling discovery also counts alias directories as packages (pm-web-cqwm). External live-fleet drift is separately tracked by pm-web-s99c. For the scoped package coverage run, use a disposable filesystem fleet fixture built from test/fleet-extensions.snapshot.json via PM_FLEET_ROOT=coverage/fleet-fixture; all catalog assertions remain enabled. This proves committed package/snapshot consistency, not live-fleet freshness. The exact failed live run remains recorded separately."
  "2026-10-05T05:36:39.174Z",codex-sol,"Added real route round trips for linked files/docs/learnings, config, import partial failures, JSON/YAML/CSV export escaping, filtered bulk previews and edits, and plan reorder/block/complete/approve/materialize/delete. Added a disposable HTTPS OIDC issuer with real discovery, PKCE verification, signed RS256 ID tokens, Basic authentication, PostgreSQL identity persistence, returning login, state rejection and code replay rejection. No production route units are mocked in these additions. Strict source/test typechecking, lint and zero-duplication gates pass; final coverage measurement is underway."
  "2026-10-05T05:37:44.743Z",codex-sol,"The mandatory linked pm test exposed inherited PM_PATH overriding cwd for direct CLI assertions in scratch projects. Added an explicit --pm-path to those fixture reads/history verification and external writes; SDK route mutations already bind their workspace root. Re-running the linked tests with source workspace context retained. This is fixture isolation, not a runtime behavior change."
  "2026-10-05T05:42:59.193Z",codex-sol,"First passing full c8 run: 485/485 tests, no skips, 67.49 seconds; statements/lines 89.79, branches 79.50, functions 93.90 across 33 src files. Compared with the same-tool resumed baseline (86.39/80.46/92.11/86.39), line/function coverage improved while branch coverage decreased as new paths entered the V8 branch denominator. Added task transition/input/shortcut tests next; thresholds will be set from the final measured run without lowering the existing gate."
